{
  "description": "Scan corpus of step 4.1 (docs/plan/steps/09-rspamd.md \u00a79). Each fixture is scanned with its trusted envelope through /checkv2 of the inbound rspamd (RSPAMD_RBL_PROFILE=test, dns-sink scan.test zones). expect.verdict and expect.reasonCodes are what the S7 mapping (R0-R10) gives with the platform defaults (spam 6, suspicious 4, phishing/DMARC-reject suspicious, auth failures reason only); expect.absentReasonCodes must not be mapped (optional), expect.symbols must be present, expect.absentSymbols absent, expect.auth is a partial match of normalizeReply().auth, expect.scoreRange is [min, max): the interval in which the score keeps the expected verdict (wide on purpose: the reputation module learns from every scan, so repeated runs move scores by up to about +/-2.5). calibrated records the values observed on rspamd/rspamd:3.12.1 (2026-11-05). The arc/ fixtures need RSPAMD_ARC_TRUSTED_SEALERS=arc-trusted.scan.test (local/CI test profile).",
  "rspamdVersion": "3.12.1",
  "platformDefaults": {
    "spamScore": 6,
    "suspiciousScore": 4,
    "phishingVerdict": "suspicious",
    "dmarcRejectVerdict": "suspicious",
    "authFailureVerdict": "reason_only"
  },
